questions.question:
A pricing service keeps its catalog in memory behind a `sync.RWMutex`:

```go
type Catalog struct {
    mu    sync.RWMutex
    items map[string]Item
    rules []Rule
}

func (c *Catalog) Price(sku string) (int64, bool) {
    c.mu.RLock()
    defer c.mu.RUnlock()
    it, ok := c.items[sku]
    if !ok {
        return 0, false
    }
    return c.ApplyRules(it), true
}

// ApplyRules is also called directly by other handlers.
func (c *Catalog) ApplyRules(it Item) int64 {
    c.mu.RLock()
    defer c.mu.RUnlock()
    p := it.BasePrice
    for _, r := range c.rules {
        p = r.Apply(p)
    }
    return p
}

// Reload runs every 30 seconds.
func (c *Catalog) Reload(items map[string]Item, rules []Rule) {
    c.mu.Lock()
    defer c.mu.Unlock()
    c.items, c.rules = items, rules
}
```

It passes every test and runs fine in staging. In production, a few hours after each deploy, all price requests hang and CPU drops to almost zero. A restart fixes it until the next time. A goroutine dump shows thousands of goroutines blocked in `sync.(*RWMutex).RLock` and one blocked in `sync.(*RWMutex).Lock` inside `Reload`. Explain what is happening and fix it.

questions.question_zh:
一个定价服务把商品目录保存在内存里，用 `sync.RWMutex` 保护：

```go
type Catalog struct {
    mu    sync.RWMutex
    items map[string]Item
    rules []Rule
}

func (c *Catalog) Price(sku string) (int64, bool) {
    c.mu.RLock()
    defer c.mu.RUnlock()
    it, ok := c.items[sku]
    if !ok {
        return 0, false
    }
    return c.ApplyRules(it), true
}

// ApplyRules is also called directly by other handlers.
func (c *Catalog) ApplyRules(it Item) int64 {
    c.mu.RLock()
    defer c.mu.RUnlock()
    p := it.BasePrice
    for _, r := range c.rules {
        p = r.Apply(p)
    }
    return p
}

// Reload runs every 30 seconds.
func (c *Catalog) Reload(items map[string]Item, rules []Rule) {
    c.mu.Lock()
    defer c.mu.Unlock()
    c.items, c.rules = items, rules
}
```

它能通过所有测试，在预发环境也运行正常。但在生产环境中，每次发布几小时后，所有价格请求都会卡住，CPU 几乎降到零。重启能恢复，直到下一次再出现。goroutine dump 显示有数千个 goroutine 阻塞在 `sync.(*RWMutex).RLock`，还有一个阻塞在 `Reload` 里的 `sync.(*RWMutex).Lock`。请解释发生了什么并修复。

questions.answer:
**Root cause: a recursive read lock meets a waiting writer.** Go's `RWMutex` prevents writer starvation: once a goroutine calls `Lock`, new `RLock` calls block until that writer has acquired and released the lock. Now take this sequence:
- Goroutine A enters `Price` and holds a read lock.
- `Reload` calls `Lock` and waits for A to release its read lock.
- A calls `ApplyRules`, which calls `RLock` again. That call now waits behind the pending writer.

A waits for the writer, and the writer waits for A. Every new request's `RLock` also queues behind the writer, so the whole service stops. The `sync` docs explicitly prohibit recursive read locking for this reason. It needs a `Reload` to land in the tiny gap between the two `RLock` calls, which is why it takes hours of production traffic and never shows up in tests.

**Why nothing reports it.** The runtime only prints `fatal error: all goroutines are asleep - deadlock!` when every goroutine is blocked. An HTTP server always has other goroutines alive, so it just hangs. The race detector does not look for deadlocks either.

**Fix 1: take the lock once, at the boundary.** Exported methods lock; unexported helpers assume the lock is already held and say so in their name, for example `applyRulesLocked`. Never call a locking method from inside a locked section. `ApplyRules` becomes a thin wrapper that locks and calls `applyRulesLocked`.

**Fix 2: use an immutable snapshot.** The data only changes in `Reload`, so readers do not need a lock at all. Publish a new snapshot with `atomic.Pointer` (Go 1.19+):

```go
type snapshot struct {
    items map[string]Item
    rules []Rule
}

type Catalog struct {
    snap atomic.Pointer[snapshot]
}

func (c *Catalog) Price(sku string) (int64, bool) {
    s := c.snap.Load()
    it, ok := s.items[sku]
    if !ok {
        return 0, false
    }
    return s.applyRules(it), true
}

func (c *Catalog) Reload(items map[string]Item, rules []Rule) {
    c.snap.Store(&snapshot{items: items, rules: rules})
}
```

Reads are lock-free, and every request sees `items` and `rules` from the same reload. The old version had a second, quieter bug here: the two separate lock acquisitions could see items from one reload and rules from the next. `Reload` must build fresh maps and never modify a published snapshot.

**Catching it earlier.** In `/debug/pprof/goroutine?debug=2`, look for one goroutine in `Lock` and many in `RLock`, with an `RLock` stack that already passed through another locked method. A stress test that calls `Reload` in a tight loop while readers run reproduces it in seconds, and libraries such as `github.com/sasha-s/go-deadlock` can flag recursive locking in CI.

questions.answer_zh:
**根本原因：递归读锁遇上了等待中的写锁。** Go 的 `RWMutex` 会防止写者饥饿：一旦有 goroutine 调用了 `Lock`，新的 `RLock` 调用就会阻塞，直到这个写者拿到锁并释放。来看这个时序：
- goroutine A 进入 `Price`，持有读锁。
- `Reload` 调用 `Lock`，等待 A 释放读锁。
- A 调用 `ApplyRules`，再次调用 `RLock`。这次调用现在要排在等待中的写者后面。

A 在等写者，写者在等 A。之后每个新请求的 `RLock` 也都排在写者后面，于是整个服务停摆。`sync` 包的文档正是因为这个原因，明确禁止递归加读锁。触发它需要 `Reload` 恰好落在两次 `RLock` 之间那个极小的空隙里，所以要在生产流量下跑上几个小时才会出现，而测试中永远看不到。

**为什么没有任何报错。** 只有当所有 goroutine 都阻塞时，运行时才会打印 `fatal error: all goroutines are asleep - deadlock!`。HTTP 服务器总有其他 goroutine 活着，所以它只会一直卡住。race detector 也不负责检测死锁。

**修复 1：只在边界加一次锁。** 导出方法负责加锁；未导出的辅助方法假定锁已被持有，并在名字里注明，例如 `applyRulesLocked`。绝不在已加锁的代码段里调用会加锁的方法。`ApplyRules` 变成一个薄包装：加锁后调用 `applyRulesLocked`。

**修复 2：使用不可变快照。** 数据只在 `Reload` 中变化，所以读者根本不需要锁。用 `atomic.Pointer`（Go 1.19+）发布新的快照：

```go
type snapshot struct {
    items map[string]Item
    rules []Rule
}

type Catalog struct {
    snap atomic.Pointer[snapshot]
}

func (c *Catalog) Price(sku string) (int64, bool) {
    s := c.snap.Load()
    it, ok := s.items[sku]
    if !ok {
        return 0, false
    }
    return s.applyRules(it), true
}

func (c *Catalog) Reload(items map[string]Item, rules []Rule) {
    c.snap.Store(&snapshot{items: items, rules: rules})
}
```

读取完全无锁，而且每个请求看到的 `items` 和 `rules` 都来自同一次 reload。旧版本在这里还有第二个更隐蔽的 bug：两次独立的加锁可能读到一次 reload 的 items 和下一次 reload 的 rules。`Reload` 必须构建全新的 map，绝不修改已经发布的快照。

**如何更早发现。** 在 `/debug/pprof/goroutine?debug=2` 中，寻找一个阻塞在 `Lock` 的 goroutine 和大量阻塞在 `RLock` 的 goroutine，其中某个 `RLock` 的调用栈已经经过了另一个加锁方法。写一个压力测试，在读者运行的同时循环调用 `Reload`，几秒内就能复现；`github.com/sasha-s/go-deadlock` 之类的库也能在 CI 中标记出递归加锁。

questions.question:
A Spring Boot service uses HikariCP with the default `maximumPoolSize=10` and Tomcat's default of 200 worker threads:

```java
@Service
public class OrderService {
    private final OrderRepository orders;
    private final AuditService audit;

    @Transactional
    public void placeOrder(Order order) {
        orders.save(order);
        audit.record(order); // @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRES_NEW)
    }
}
```

The audit record must survive even if the order rolls back, hence `REQUIRES_NEW`. Load tests with 5 concurrent users pass. During a flash sale the service freezes: every request fails after 30 s with `SQLTransientConnectionException: HikariPool-1 - Connection is not available, request timed out after 30000ms`, yet the database shows 10 open connections doing nothing and almost no CPU. Explain what is happening and fix it.

questions.question_zh:
一个 Spring Boot 服务使用 HikariCP，连接池保持默认的 `maximumPoolSize=10`，Tomcat 也是默认的 200 个工作线程：

```java
@Service
public class OrderService {
    private final OrderRepository orders;
    private final AuditService audit;

    @Transactional
    public void placeOrder(Order order) {
        orders.save(order);
        audit.record(order); // @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRES_NEW)
    }
}
```

即使订单回滚，审计记录也必须保留，所以用了 `REQUIRES_NEW`。5 个并发用户的压测能通过。但在一次限时抢购中，服务卡死了：每个请求都在 30 s 后失败，报 `SQLTransientConnectionException: HikariPool-1 - Connection is not available, request timed out after 30000ms`，而数据库那边只有 10 个什么都不做的连接，CPU 几乎为零。请解释发生了什么并修复。
